 objectives oh  two  active learning  teaching is teaching  whether you're doing it the way we're  communicating now to each other or  whether you're doing it in a traditional  live classroom  or whether it's a hybrid you're doing  some of this and some of that  there are advantages to one of these  environments  and disadvantages and conversely for the  other environment there are some things  that you can do better online  than you can in an additional  mode  let's just consider lecture all right  straight lecture i get up and give a  lecture in a class and i'm traditional  i'm talking at the students for 50  minutes or 75 minutes and they're  listening and maybe they're asking  questions maybe they're just sitting  there passively receiving information  maybe they're not even passively  receiving information  they're focusing more on the cell phone  which is in their lap that they're busy  texting a friend or whatever may be  going on all right so that's the  traditional approach  the online approach is now instead of  giving a lecture  in a classroom to students i videotape  the lecture  all right and the students  watch the taped lecture in the comfort  of their uh their own home or dormitory  room or wherever there is  i'm going to argue that the  not much learning is going to happen  either way  right because it's a straight lecture  there's no active involvement there's no  desirable difficulty it's just passive  reception of information  but i'm guessing that the online  approach is going to be more effective  than the traditional lecture approach  why because the student has some control  in the online environment  if i say something which is  incomprehensible to the student just  flies right past them they can stop  rewind play it again  and they can do that as many times as  they need to until  it either becomes clear to them or they  have a question that they can formulate  and send to the professor in whatever  mode of communication they have or if  th